afk: brainstorming blocks its todo phase for the duration of the dialogue.

Motivation: the harness sends a stop-time reminder whenever an assistant
turn ends with pending/in_progress todos (omp
packages/coding-agent/src/session/todo-tracker.ts, checkCompletion), plus
a mid-run nudge after 12 mutating tool calls (takeMidRunNudge). This
skill mandates a task per checklist item AND one question per message,
so every brainstorming turn trips it: the agent gets nudged toward
execution in the middle of a design conversation.

`blocked` is the existing, documented state for "open but waiting on
external input", and both reminder paths filter to pending/in_progress
only, so blocking the phase suppresses them without disabling reminders
globally or touching omp. A forgotten unblock cannot strand the list on
the architectural path: writing-plans opens with a fresh `todo init`,
which replaces the phases outright. The spike and bounded paths (upstream
v6.3.0 three-path router) never reach writing-plans, so their own
post-approval step carries the unblock.

What must survive a rebase:
- The block instruction sits with the checklist preamble (after "create a
  task for each item on your path"), so it runs before the first turn
  that can end with open todos, whichever path was classified.
- Every path unblocks at its first post-approval step: spike step 4
  (Investigate), bounded step 5 (Implement), architectural step 9
  (transition to implementation, before handing off to writing-plans).
- Document-reviewer template dispatches the `reviewer` agent (task
  tool), never `general-purpose` — no such agent exists here.

